  "description": "The 2026 race for Maryland's 2nd Congressional District features incumbent Democrat Johnny Olszewski, first elected in 2024 with 58.2% of the vote. The district encompasses much of Baltimore County, Carroll County, and portions of Baltimore City, with a Cook Partisan Voter Index of D+10, and is rated 'Solid D' by the Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, and Sabato's Crystal Ball. Olszewski faces a Democratic primary challenge from Clint Spellman Jr., a Marine Corps veteran and insurance agent. On the Republican side, perennial candidates Nnabu Eze and Dave Wallace are competing for their party's nomination. The primary elections are scheduled for June 23, 2026, with the general election on November 3, 2026.",
